# Portfolio chatbot

Interactive portfolio for Daniel A Rodrigues. Users chat to learn about professional experience and some personal background. Current features: streaming chat (OpenRouter via Route Handlers), MongoDB-backed threaded messages with TTL, resume download.

## Stack

- Next.js 15 App Router, React 19, TypeScript (strict)
- Tailwind + shadcn/ui (`new-york`, zinc CSS variables)
- Backend: Route Handlers under `src/app/api/v1` + `src/server/` (MongoDB, OpenRouter)
- HTTP (client): native `fetch` + ReadableStream for chat SSE
- Path alias: `@/` → `src/`

## Layout

- UI: `@src/app/components/ui/` (shadcn primitives + chatbot/header)
- App shell: `@src/app/page.tsx`, `@src/app/layout.tsx`
- API routes: `@src/app/api/v1/`
- Server logic: `@src/server/` (`db/`, `chat/`, `ai/`)
- Client API helpers: `@src/shared/` (`api.ts`, `endpoints.ts`, `config.ts`)
- Hooks: `@src/hooks/`
- Utils: `@src/lib/utils.ts` (`cn`)

## Guardrails

- Extend `@src/shared/` for browser→API calls; do not invent parallel fetch wrappers
- Put server-only backend logic under `@src/server/` and Route Handlers under `@src/app/api/`
- Preserve the dark zinc chat UX unless explicitly redesigning
- LLM calls go through OpenRouter (see `@v2-migration.mdc`); never put API keys in client code
- Do not reintroduce Telegram notify or title-generation endpoints unless explicitly requested
- CI runs lint, typecheck, and build on PRs and `main` (see `.github/workflows/ci.yml`); use the PR template for release-oriented descriptions
